changes_in_r4:
  - F-04 P1: the legacy single-destination path applies ONLY when DESTINATIONS is absent. Present
    but empty ("", whitespace, null) is invalid configuration and acceptance fails closed with 503
  - F-05 P2: a PRESENT timeout_ms (and retry field) is validated instead of falling through to the
    default: 0, null, false and "" are invalid, not 10000 by omission
  - R21: GC contract stated precisely -- the failed sequence is resolved, but the backlog a halted
    destination is still owed stays durable until retry/skip; other Hubs keep operating
changes_in_r3:
  - F-02B P1: a disabled destination no longer pins global GC. Heads are reconciled for every known
    destination (never past a real pending delivery, a FAILED_PERMANENT or a halt), so its retention
    frontier advances over sequences it was never owed
  - F-03B P1: `enabled`, when present, must be a strict boolean. "false", 0, null and any other type
    are invalid configuration and acceptance fails closed with 503
  - docs: `outbox` described precisely (evidence preserved; only the resolution state of a migrated
    legacy row is mirrored, per F-05); R8.2.3.3 is the CONTRACT BASELINE, the operating Hub is R8.4 REV8
changes_in_r2:
  - F-02 (re-audit): enabled/disabled authority moved to the Sequencer. A disabled destination's
    pending deliveries are resolved at dispatch AND at claim time, and nothing is published to its
    queue; the consumer-side check remains a secondary defence. No dependency on config sync
    between Workers.
  - docs: disabling a destination no longer implies redeploying its consumer; the rollback section
    now states that resolutions of migrated legacy rows are mirrored into `outbox` (F-05)
